2828 0 obj
<</Alt(\nLearn the fundamentals of the OpenCV library in Python: \nsetting up the development environment, installing OpenCV via pip,\nunderstanding how images are stored as NumPy arrays, and practicing core functions such as cv2.imread\(\), cv2.imshow\(\), cv2.imwrite\(\), and cv2.waitKey\(\) to read, display, and save images in different formats.\n\n)/K 2829 0 R /P 822 0 R /S/Annot>>
endobj
2829 0 obj
<</Obj 2342 0 R /P 2828 0 R /Pg 15 0 R /Type/OBJR>>
endobj
2830 0 obj
<</AP<</N 3896 0 R >>/BS<</S/N/Type/Border/W 0>>/C[]/CA 1/Contents(\nStudy color space theory and conversions between BGR, Grayscale, and HSV using cv2.cvtColor\(\); \npractice image resizing with cv2.resize\(\) using different interpolation methods;\nlearn region-of-interest cropping via NumPy slicing; \ndraw shapes and annotations using cv2.line\(\), cv2.rectangle\(\), cv2.circle\(\), and cv2.putText\(\); apply binary and adaptive thresholding using cv2.threshold\(\) and cv2.adaptiveThreshold\(\) including Otsu's method; \nreduce image noise using smoothing filters such as cv2.blur\(\), cv2.GaussianBlur\(\), cv2.medianBlur\(\), \nand finally cv2.bilateralFilter\(\).\n)/CreationDate(D:20260503083637Z)/DA(/Helvetica 13 Tf 0 0 0 rg )/DS(font:13.00pt "Helvetica"; color:#000000; )/F 4/FontName(Helvetica)/FontSize 13/M(D:20260503083806Z)/NM(01KQPFPYJCN9ARRXVAF2HVA9HJ)/P 15 0 R /PSPDF:Id(7KQ22VJQ029Q3E7DP2RSSX7M5K)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:spec="2.0.2"><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">\nStudy color space theory and conversions between BGR, Grayscale, and HSV using cv2.cvtColor\(\); </span></p><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">practice image resizing with cv2.resize\(\) using different interpolation methods;</span></p><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">learn region-of-interest cropping via NumPy slicing; </span></p><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">draw shapes and annotations using cv2.line\(\), cv2.rectangle\(\), cv2.circle\(\), and cv2.putText\(\); apply binary and adaptive thresholding using cv2.threshold\(\) and cv2.adaptiveThreshold\(\) including Otsu&#39;s method; </span></p><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">reduce image noise using smoothing filters such as cv2.blur\(\), cv2.GaussianBlur\(\), cv2.medianBlur\(\), </span></p><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">and finally cv2.bilateralFilter\(\).\n</span></p></body>)/Rect[ 50.757862 362.7684 584.75787 545.76843]/Resources<<>>/StructParent 101/Subtype/FreeText/Type/Annot>>
endobj
3245 0 obj
<</Alt(\nStudy color space theory and conversions between BGR, Grayscale, and HSV using cv2.cvtColor\(\); practice image resizing with cv2.resize\(\) using different interpolation methods; learn region-of-interest cropping via NumPy slicing; draw shapes and annotations using cv2.line\(\), cv2.rectangle\(\), cv2.circle\(\), and cv2.putText\(\); apply binary and adaptive thresholding using cv2.threshold\(\) and cv2.adaptiveThreshold\(\) including Otsu's method; reduce image noise using smoothing filters such as cv2.blur\(\), cv2.GaussianBlur\(\), cv2.medianBlur\(\), and cv2.bilateralFilter\(\).\n)/K 3246 0 R /P 839 0 R /S/Annot>>
endobj
