8314 0 obj
<</Alt(\nStudy edge detection theory and apply the Canny algorithm using cv2.Canny\(\) with different threshold values to understand how sensitivity changes; \nalso apply the Sobel operator using cv2.Sobel\(\) in both X and Y directions and combine the results to compute gradient magnitude; then practice contour detection using cv2.findContours\(\) with different retrieval modes,\ndraw contours with cv2.drawContours\(\), and compute geometric properties such as area using cv2.contourArea\(\), perimeter using cv2.arcLength\(\), and bounding rectangles using cv2.boundingRect\(\).\n)/K 8315 0 R /P 899 0 R /S/Annot>>
endobj
8315 0 obj
<</Obj 7150 0 R /P 8314 0 R /Pg 17 0 R /Type/OBJR>>
endobj
8316 0 obj
<</AP<</N 9000 0 R >>/BS<</S/N/Type/Border/W 0>>/C[]/CA 1/Contents(\nExplore morphological image processing by creating custom structuring elements with cv2.getStructuringElement\(\) and \napplying erosion using cv2.erode\(\), dilation using cv2.dilate\(\), \nmorphological opening and closing using cv2.morphologyEx\(\); \nthen study image histograms using cv2.calcHist\(\) and visualize them with matplotlib; apply global histogram equalization using cv2.equalizeHist\(\) \nand compare it with CLAHE \(Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization\) using cv2.createCLAHE\(\) on images with different lighting conditions.\n)/CreationDate(D:20260503084132Z)/DA(/Helvetica 13 Tf 0 0 0 rg )/DS(font:13.00pt "Helvetica"; color:#000000; )/F 4/FontName(Helvetica)/FontSize 13/M(D:20260503084207Z)/NM(01KQPFZZGJSDHWMXKFP3WSXKT3)/P 17 0 R /PSPDF:Id(7KQ22VJQ0747TCF4H0XCT9XJ6B)/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:spec="2.0.2"><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">\nExplore morphological image processing by creating custom structuring elements with cv2.getStructuringElement\(\) and </span></p><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">applying erosion using cv2.erode\(\), dilation using cv2.dilate\(\), </span></p><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">morphological opening and closing using cv2.morphologyEx\(\); </span></p><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">then study image histograms using cv2.calcHist\(\) and visualize them with matplotlib; apply global histogram equalization using cv2.equalizeHist\(\) </span></p><p style="font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-size:13px;font-family:Helvetica;text-align:initial">and compare it with CLAHE \(Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization\) using cv2.createCLAHE\(\) on images with different lighting conditions.\n</span></p></body>)/Rect[ 19.263159 372.55804 611.26318 525.55804]/Resources<<>>/StructParent 105/Subtype/FreeText/Type/Annot>>
endobj
8710 0 obj
<</Alt(\nExplore morphological image processing by creating custom structuring elements with cv2.getStructuringElement\(\) and applying erosion using cv2.erode\(\), dilation using cv2.dilate\(\), morphological opening and closing using cv2.morphologyEx\(\); then study image histograms using cv2.calcHist\(\) and visualize them with matplotlib; apply global histogram equalization using cv2.equalizeHist\(\) and compare it with CLAHE \(Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization\) using cv2.createCLAHE\(\) on images with different lighting conditions.\n)/K 8711 0 R /P 914 0 R /S/Annot>>
endobj
8711 0 obj
<</Obj 8316 0 R /P 8710 0 R /Pg 17 0 R /Type/OBJR>>
